public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.Cotangent.DerivedPushoutBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.Cotangent.PolynomialRetraction
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Augmentation

/-!
# The cotangent complex of a quotient by a Koszul-regular sequence

Let `R → S` be a surjective ring map whose kernel is generated by a Koszul-regular sequence
`f₁, …, f_r ∈ R`. Then `L_{S/R}` is quasi-isomorphic to the conormal module `I/I²` placed in
cohomological degree `-1`; this is [Stacks, Tag 08SJ]. This file proves it with Proposition 08QX,
for the towers `R → P → R` with `P` a polynomial algebra over `R` carrying a retraction, taken as
a parameter (this file is upstream of Proposition 08QX); the statement under exactly the source's
hypotheses, which carries the tag, is
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence_unconditional` of
`StacksFrontier.Cotangent.KoszulRegularQuotientUnconditional`.

The proof is the source's. Write `P = R[x₁, …, x_r]` and send `x_i` to `f_i`, giving `P → R`;
send every `x_i` to `0`, giving `P → R` again — the augmentation. Then

```
P  --→  R
|       |
R  --→  S
```

commutes, the Koszul-regularity of `f` makes `R` and the augmented copy of `R` Tor independent
over `P` (`MvPolynomial.torIndependent_aeval_augmentation`), and `S = R ⊗_P R`
(`MvPolynomial.isPushout_aeval_augmentation`); so the square induces a quasi-isomorphism
`R ⊗_P^𝐋 R = S` and [Stacks, Tag 08QQ] applies, in the form
`CommAlgCat.derivedCotangentComplexBaseChangeIso`:

`L_{S/R} = L_{R/P} ⊗^𝐋_R S`.

The left vertical map is the augmentation of a polynomial algebra, so [Stacks, Tag 08SI] computes
`L_{R/P}`: it is a *projective* module in degree `-1`
(`CommAlgCat.exists_projective_cotangentComplex_retraction_iso_single`, the quantitative form of
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_retraction_iso_single`). Derived extension of scalars
carries a single projective module to a single module in the same degree
(`CommAlgCat.totalDerivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfProjective`), so `L_{S/R}` is a single module
in degree `-1`, hence has no cohomology in the degrees `≤ -2` — and that single vanishing is all
that `StacksFrontier.Cotangent.SurjectionSingleDegree` needs in order to identify `L_{S/R}` with
`I/I²[1]`.

## Main definitions

* `CommAlgCat.totalDerivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfProjective`: total derived extension of
  scalars sends a projective module placed in degree `n` to its base change placed in degree `n`.

## Main results

* `CommAlgCat.exists_projective_cotangentComplex_retraction_iso_single`: for the augmentation
  `B → A` of a polynomial algebra `B` over `A`, the complex `L_{A/B}` is isomorphic in `D(A)` to
  a *projective* `A`-module placed in cohomological degree `-1`, namely `A ⊗_B Ω[B⁄A]`.
* `CommAlgCat.isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence`:
  `H^i(L_{S/R}) = 0` for `i ≤ -2`, when `ker(R → S)` is generated by a Koszul-regular sequence.
* `CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence`:
  [Stacks, Tag 08SJ] with Proposition 08QX at the towers `R → P → R` as a parameter.

## The carried hypothesis

Proposition 08QX — that the three vertices of the display of Tag 08QS form a distinguished
triangle for arbitrary ring maps `A → B → C` — is proved downstream of this file, as
`CommAlgCat.productFundamentalTriangle_distinguished` of
`StacksFrontier.Cotangent.Triangle.ProductDescent`, and read as `CommAlgCat.hasFundamentalTriangleAt`
in `StacksFrontier.Cotangent.PolynomialRetractionUnconditional`. Tag 08SI in the form
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_retraction_iso_single` carries it as the explicit
hypothesis `CommAlgCat.HasFundamentalTriangleAt A B A`, and so does everything here;
`StacksFrontier.Cotangent.KoszulRegularQuotientUnconditional` discharges it.

The hypothesis is carried in the form

`∀ P, Algebra.IsPolynomialAlgebra R P → HasFundamentalTriangleAt R P R`,

quantified over the polynomial algebras `P` over `R` carrying a retraction `P → R`. Quantifying
is what lets the hypothesis be stated at all: the tower whose triangle the proof needs is
`R → R[x₁, …, x_r] → R`, whose middle-to-right map is the augmentation `x_i ↦ 0`, and that is not
the `Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin r) R) R` structure of any instance — it is one of *two*
structures the proof puts on the pair, the other being `x_i ↦ f_i`. The quantified form names
neither, and is the weakest hypothesis that can be written without an instance for the
augmentation.

Carrying it does not turn the statement into a restatement of its own conclusion: the hypothesis
asserts only that a distinguished triangle exists on three named vertices, for towers
`R → P → R` with `P` a polynomial algebra, and says nothing about the cotangent complex of
`R → S`. The three inputs that make the conclusion — Tag 08QQ, Tag 08QH for `L_{P/R}`, and the
Tor independence coming from the Koszul-regularity of `f` — are all proved.

## Tag 08SK

[Stacks, Tag 08SK] is the same conclusion for a kernel that is a Koszul-regular *ideal* in the
sense of Tag 07CV (2), `Ideal.IsKoszulRegular`. That predicate supplies a Koszul-regular
generating sequence only after localizing: it gives, at each prime containing the ideal, some
`g` outside it and a Koszul-regular sequence generating the ideal in `Localization.Away g`
(`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Regular/Ideal.lean:75`). Deducing the global vanishing of
`H^i(L_{S/R})` from the local one needs the comparison of `L_{S/R}` with the cotangent complexes
of the localizations, which is [Stacks, Tag 08SF] (`cotangent-lemma-localize`), not imported here.
Tag 08SK is therefore proved downstream, in `StacksFrontier.Cotangent.KoszulRegularIdealQuotient`
(with Tag 08SF and Proposition 08QX as parameters) and
`StacksFrontier.Cotangent.KoszulRegularIdealQuotientUnconditional` (under the source's hypotheses).

## Implementation notes

**The two algebra structures on one ring.** `P = R[x₁, …, x_r]` maps to `R` twice, by `x_i ↦ f_i`
and by `x_i ↦ 0`, and the square of Tag 08QQ uses both at once. Two `Algebra P R` instances
cannot coexist, so the work is done in
`CommAlgCat.isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence_aux`, where the base of
the polynomial algebra is a *separate* variable `k` and only one structure is put on each of `k`
and `R`; the public statements instantiate `k := R`. Nothing is lost by the generality, and
nothing is gained either: it is a device for naming both structures at once. In particular no
`ULift` of the base ring is needed — the hypothesis and the conclusion speak only of `R`.

**The projective module, not the conormal module.** Tag 08SI as stated in the library concludes
with the conormal module `I/I²` of the augmentation, about which nothing says it is projective;
the proof of Tag 08SI goes through `L_{A/B} ≅ (L_{B/A} ⊗^𝐋_B A)[1]` and the first vertex *is* a
projective module in degree `0`, by Tag 08QH and the projectivity of `Ω[B⁄A]`. Derived extension
of scalars is applied to that vertex here, so
`CommAlgCat.exists_projective_cotangentComplex_retraction_iso_single` re-runs the triangle step
of `CommAlgCat.isGE_cotangentComplexDerived_retraction` and keeps the module, rather than
consuming the conclusion of Tag 08SI.

**One lemma for two functors.** `CommAlgCat.cotangentComplexDerivedBaseChange` is built from
`CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.totalDerivedExtensionScalars` and Tag 08QQ from
`CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral`; in one universe the
latter is the former, and both are inhabitants of
`CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.TotalDerivedExtensionScalars`, so
`CommAlgCat.totalDerivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfProjective` is stated for an arbitrary
inhabitant and serves both. It has two near-neighbours in the library, neither of which serves:
`CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.derivedExtensionScalarsSingleIso` of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/ExtendScalars/DerivedHomology.lean` is for a *flat* ring map and only in
degree `0`, and the homonymous lemma of
`StacksFrontier/Cotangent/StandardResolutionOverPolynomialBase.lean` is for a projective module but
only in degree `0`, only for `derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral`, and is `private` to that module.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08SJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08SJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08SI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08SI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08SK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08SK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08SF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08SF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08QQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08QQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08QS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08QS), the displayed triangle.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08QX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08QX), that it is distinguished.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08QH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08QH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07CV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07CV)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated

universe u

namespace CommAlgCat

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **Total derived extension of scalars of a projective module in a single degree.** A single
complex on a projective module is a bounded-above complex of projectives, so the comparison from
derived to termwise extension of scalars is invertible at it; termwise extension of scalars
leaves a complex concentrated in degree `n` concentrated in degree `n`.

The statement is for an arbitrary inhabitant of
`CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.TotalDerivedExtensionScalars`, so that it applies both to
`CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.totalDerivedExtensionScalars`, out of which
`CommAlgCat.cotangentComplexDerivedBaseChange` is built, and to
`CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral`, which is the functor of
[Stacks, Tag 08QQ]. -/
def totalDerivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfProjective
    {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (f : R →+* S)
    (D : CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.TotalDerivedExtensionScalars.{u, u, u} f)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) [Projective M] (n : ℤ) :
    D.functor.obj ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj M) ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} S) n).obj
        ((ModuleCat.extendScalars f).obj M) := by
  let _ := D.additive
  let F := ModuleCat.extendScalars.{u, u, u} f
  let P := (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj M
  have hstrict : P.IsStrictlyLE n := inferInstance
  have hproj : ∀ i : ℤ, Projective (P.X i) := by
    intro i
    rcases eq_or_ne i n with rfl | hi
    · exact Projective.of_iso
        (HomologicalComplex.singleObjXSelf (ComplexShape.up ℤ) i M).symm inferInstance
    · exact (HomologicalComplex.isZero_single_obj_X (ComplexShape.up ℤ) n M i hi).projective
  have := hproj
  have := hstrict
  have hcomp : IsIso (D.comparison.app P) := D.comparison_isIso_of_projective P n
  exact (D.functor.mapIso ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).app M)) ≪≫
    @asIso _ _ _ _ _ hcomp ≪≫
    DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso
      ((HomologicalComplex.singleMapHomologicalComplex F (ComplexShape.up ℤ) n).app M) ≪≫
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ (ModuleCat.{u} S) n).app (F.obj M)).symm

section Retraction

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Algebra B A]
  [IsScalarTower A B A]

/-- **`L_{A/B}` is a projective module in degree `-1`, for the augmentation `B → A` of a
polynomial algebra `B` over `A`.** The fundamental triangle of `A → B → A` has zero middle
vertex, since `L_{A/A} = 0`, so its connecting morphism identifies `L_{A/B}` with the shift of
the first vertex `L_{B/A} ⊗^𝐋_B A`; by [Stacks, Tag 08QH] the complex `L_{B/A}` is the single
complex on the free module `Ω[B⁄A]`, so that vertex is `A ⊗_B Ω[B⁄A]` in degree `0`
(`CommAlgCat.totalDerivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfProjective`), and extension of scalars
preserves projectivity.

This is the quantitative form of `CommAlgCat.isGE_cotangentComplexDerived_retraction`: the module
is produced, not only the degree bound. The hypothesis `h08QX` is Proposition 08QX for the tower
`A → B → A`; see the module docstring. -/
theorem exists_projective_cotangentComplex_retraction_iso_single
    (hB : Algebra.IsPolynomialAlgebra A B) (h08QX : HasFundamentalTriangleAt A B A) :
    ∃ M : ModuleCat.{u} ↥(CommAlgCat.of B A), Projective M ∧
      Nonempty (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cotangentComplex B (CommAlgCat.of B A)) ≅
        (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} ↥(CommAlgCat.of B A)) (-1)).obj M) := by
  obtain ⟨α, β, δ, hT⟩ := h08QX
  have h₂ : IsZero (cotangentComplexDerived A (CommAlgCat.of A A)) :=
    isZero_cotangentComplex_self A
  have hiso : IsIso δ := (Triangle.isZero₂_iff_isIso₃ (Triangle.mk α β δ) hT).1 h₂
  have hproj : Module.Projective ↥(CommAlgCat.of A B)
      (KaehlerDifferential A ↥(CommAlgCat.of A B)) :=
    KaehlerDifferential.projective_of_isPolynomialAlgebra hB
  have := hproj
  let Ω := ModuleCat.of ↥(CommAlgCat.of A B) (KaehlerDifferential A ↥(CommAlgCat.of A B))
  have hΩ : Projective Ω := inferInstance
  have := hΩ
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := cotangentComplex_iso_kaehlerDifferential A (CommAlgCat.of A B) hB
  let D := CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.totalDerivedExtensionScalars
    (algebraMap ↥(CommAlgCat.of A B) A)
  let M := (ModuleCat.extendScalars (algebraMap ↥(CommAlgCat.of A B) A)).obj Ω
  refine ⟨M, (ModuleCat.extendRestrictScalarsAdj
    (algebraMap ↥(CommAlgCat.of A B) A)).map_projective Ω hΩ, ⟨?_⟩⟩
  exact @asIso _ _ _ _ _ hiso ≪≫ (shiftFunctor _ (1 : ℤ)).mapIso
      (D.functor.mapIso e ≪≫
        totalDerivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfProjective _ D Ω 0) ≪≫
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctors (ModuleCat.{u} A)).shiftIso 1 (-1) 0 (by omega)).app M

end Retraction

section KoszulRegular

/-- **The vanishing of [Stacks, Tag 08SJ], with the base of the polynomial algebra kept
separate.** For a `k`-algebra `R`, a quotient `S` of `R` by the ideal generated by a
Koszul-regular sequence `f₁, …, f_r ∈ R`, the complex `L_{S/R}` has no cohomology in the degrees
`≤ -2`.

The square of `P = k[x₁, …, x_r] → R`, `x_i ↦ f_i` over `P → k`, `x_i ↦ 0` induces a
quasi-isomorphism `R ⊗_P^𝐋 k = S` — Tor independence by
`MvPolynomial.torIndependent_aeval_augmentation` and the pushout by
`MvPolynomial.isPushout_aeval_augmentation` — so [Stacks, Tag 08QQ] identifies `L_{S/R}` with
`L_{k/P} ⊗^𝐋_k S`, and `L_{k/P}` is a projective module in degree `-1`.

`k` is a separate variable only so that the two `P`-algebra structures on `R` can be named at
once; the public statements take `k = R`. -/
private theorem isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence_aux
    (k R : Type u) [CommRing k] [CommRing R] [Algebra k R] (S : CommAlgCat.{u} R)
    [Algebra k (S : Type u)] [IsScalarTower k R (S : Type u)]
    (h : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R (S : Type u)))
    {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (hf : Koszul.IsKoszulRegular f)
    (hI : RingHom.ker (algebraMap R (S : Type u)) = Ideal.span (Set.range f))
    (h08QX : ∀ (T : Type u) [CommRing T] [Algebra k T] [Algebra T k] [IsScalarTower k T k],
      Algebra.IsPolynomialAlgebra k T → HasFundamentalTriangleAt k T k)
    (i : ℤ) (hi : i ≤ -2) :
    IsZero ((cotangentComplex R S).homology i) := by
  let P := MvPolynomial (Fin r) k
  let _ : Algebra P k :=
    (MvPolynomial.aeval (0 : Fin r → k) : P →ₐ[k] k).toRingHom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra P R := (MvPolynomial.aeval f : P →ₐ[k] R).toRingHom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra P (S : Type u) :=
    ((algebraMap R (S : Type u)).comp
      (MvPolynomial.aeval f : P →ₐ[k] R).toRingHom).toAlgebra
  let _ : IsScalarTower P R (S : Type u) := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  let _ : IsScalarTower P k (S : Type u) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (MvPolynomial.algebraMap_comp_aeval_eq k R (S : Type u) f hI)
  let _ : IsScalarTower k P k :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (RingHom.ext fun c => by
      change algebraMap k k c = MvPolynomial.aeval (0 : Fin r → k) (MvPolynomial.C c)
      simp)
  have hpoly : Algebra.IsPolynomialAlgebra k P :=
    ⟨ULift.{u} (Fin r), ⟨MvPolynomial.renameEquiv k Equiv.ulift⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨M, hM, ⟨eM⟩⟩ :=
    exists_projective_cotangentComplex_retraction_iso_single k P hpoly (h08QX P hpoly)
  have hTor : RingTheory.TorIndependence.TorIndependent P R (↥(CommAlgCat.of P k)) :=
    MvPolynomial.torIndependent_aeval_augmentation k R f hf
  let _ : Algebra.IsPushout P (↥(CommAlgCat.of P k)) R (S : Type u) :=
    (MvPolynomial.isPushout_aeval_augmentation k R (S : Type u) h f hI).symm
  let b : (↥(CommAlgCat.of P k)) →ₐ[P] (S : Type u) := IsScalarTower.toAlgHom P k (S : Type u)
  have hφ : Function.Bijective (baseChangeUnit b) :=
    bijective_baseChangeUnit_of_isPushout b (fun _ => rfl)
  have e08QQ := derivedCotangentComplexBaseChangeIso (A := P) (A' := R)
    (B := CommAlgCat.of P k) (B' := S) b hTor hφ
  let D := CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral b.toRingHom
  have efinal : DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cotangentComplex R S) ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} (S : Type u)) (-1)).obj
        ((ModuleCat.extendScalars b.toRingHom).obj M) :=
    e08QQ.symm ≪≫ D.functor.mapIso eM ≪≫
      totalDerivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfProjective b.toRingHom D M (-1)
  have : (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cotangentComplex R S)).IsGE (-1) :=
    DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.isGE_of_iso efinal.symm (-1)
  refine (DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE
    (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cotangentComplex R S)) (-1) i (by omega)).of_iso ?_
  exact ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors
    (ModuleCat.{u} (S : Type u)) i).app (cotangentComplex R S)).symm

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (S : CommAlgCat.{u} R)

/-- **`H^i(L_{S/R}) = 0` for `i ≤ -2`**, when `R → S` is surjective with kernel generated by a
Koszul-regular sequence. This is the one vanishing that
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isZero_homology_le_negTwo` needs, and the
whole content of [Stacks, Tag 08SJ].

The hypothesis `h08QX` is Proposition 08QX for the towers `R → P → R` with `P` a polynomial
algebra over `R` carrying a retraction; see the module docstring. -/
theorem isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence
    (h : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R (S : Type u)))
    {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (hf : Koszul.IsKoszulRegular f)
    (hI : RingHom.ker (algebraMap R (S : Type u)) = Ideal.span (Set.range f))
    (h08QX : ∀ (P : Type u) [CommRing P] [Algebra R P] [Algebra P R] [IsScalarTower R P R],
      Algebra.IsPolynomialAlgebra R P → HasFundamentalTriangleAt R P R)
    (i : ℤ) (hi : i ≤ -2) :
    IsZero ((cotangentComplex R S).homology i) :=
  isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence_aux R R S h f hf hI h08QX i hi

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 08SJ] with Proposition 08QX as a parameter.** Let `R → S` be a surjective map
of commutative rings whose kernel `I` is generated by a Koszul-regular sequence
`f₁, …, f_r ∈ R`, and assume `h08QX`, Proposition 08QX for the towers `R → P → R` with `P` a
polynomial algebra over `R` carrying a retraction. Then `L_{S/R}` is quasi-isomorphic to
`I/I²[1]`, that is, isomorphic in `D(S)` to the conormal module `I/I²` placed in cohomological
degree `-1`.

The source's proof: the square of `P = R[x₁, …, x_r] → R`, `x_i ↦ f_i` over the augmentation
`P → R`, `x_i ↦ 0` induces a quasi-isomorphism `R ⊗_P^𝐋 R = S`, so [Stacks, Tag 08QQ] reduces the
computation to `L_{R/P}`, which [Stacks, Tag 08SI] gives as a projective module in degree `-1`.
Hence `L_{S/R}` has no cohomology in the degrees `≤ -2`, and
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isZero_homology_le_negTwo` concludes.

The hypothesis `h08QX` is discharged, and the tag registered, in
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence_unconditional`. -/
theorem nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence
    (h : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R (S : Type u)))
    {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R) (hf : Koszul.IsKoszulRegular f)
    (hI : RingHom.ker (algebraMap R (S : Type u)) = Ideal.span (Set.range f))
    (h08QX : ∀ (P : Type u) [CommRing P] [Algebra R P] [Algebra P R] [IsScalarTower R P R],
      Algebra.IsPolynomialAlgebra R P → HasFundamentalTriangleAt R P R) :
    Nonempty (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cotangentComplex R S) ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} (S : Type u)) (-1)).obj
        (ModuleCat.of (S : Type u) (surjectionExtension R S h).Cotangent)) :=
  nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isZero_homology_le_negTwo R S h
    (isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence R S h f hf hI h08QX)

end KoszulRegular

end CommAlgCat

end
